**WELCOME TO OLX** **At OLX, we work together to build a more sustainable world through trade**.
We make it safe, smart, and convenient to buy and sell cars, find housing, get jobs, buy and sell household goods, and more. Our colleagues around the world help to serve millions of people around the world every month, through its well\-loved consumer brands including OLX, Otodom, AutoTrader, Property24\.**Join OLX and see how far you can go**. **WELCOME TO OLX GROUP**  

We work together to build a more sustainable world through trade. We make it safe, smart, and convenient to buy and sell cars, find housing, get jobs, buy and sell household goods, and more. Our colleagues around the world help to serve millions of people around the world every month, through its well\-loved consumer brands including OLX, Otodom, Imovirtual, Storia.  

At OLX, we invest in ourselves and each other to reach our full potential. We avoid bureaucracy and empower our teams to innovate; with opportunities, training, and leadership behaviors a key focus for all. Our commitment to inclusion ensures we listen to a diverse range of voices when making decisions. And, we combine the spirit and agility of a startup with our global scale and the backing of Prosus, one of the largest consumer internet groups in the world.  

Join OLX and see how far you can go. **About the role**  

The role is hybrid, available in Poland and Portugal with Poznań, Warsaw and Lisbon as preferred locations.  



As a part of EU CRM Marketing team you will be responsible for shaping the strategy and together with a team of 3 CRM Marketing Managers and Specialists **growing engagement and retention across our Vertical brands (Real Estate \& Motors): Otodom, Otomoto (PL), Imovirtual, Standvirtual (PT) and Storia, Autovit (RO).** **This role will require you to shape the right strategy to grow user engagement on both seller and buyer sides, taking regional and cross\-business\-unit scalability into consideration.** You will have an opportunity to lead expansion of CRM technical capabilities launching new CRM tools in cooperation with the MarTech team and to design right measurement frameworks with Analytics and Data Science. Working as EU CRM Marketing Lead you will shape and lead the cross\-functional collaboration with senior stakeholders, ensuring alignment with other teams including Performance \& Brand Marketing, MarTech, Product, as well as EU CRM marketers responsible for other platforms. You will serve as a thought leader for CRM Marketing Managers and Specialists, fostering an ongoing testing and experimentation culture, making sure new advanced marketing automation solutions are effectively explored and implemented.  

The envisioned ideal profile for this role is a **senior CRM professional with a strong strategic and stakeholder management experience in a cross\-functional environment**. Having a strong project management skill set will enable you in this role to lead complex, international projects impacting millions of users.  

You will report to the Head of CRM Marketing for Europe. The EU CRM Marketing team contains approximately 10 people and is an integrated part of the EU Marketing organisation.
### **What will you be doing?**

* Development and coordination of delivery of CRM Marketing strategy for Verticals aimed at growing engagement and retention across Real Estate \& Motors platforms: Otodom, Otomoto (PL), Imovirtual, Standvirtual (PT) and Storia, Autovit (RO);
* Leading role in launch of a new CRM tool in cooperation with the MarTech team across all Verticals brands, ensuring key marketing needs are effectively addressed;
* Owning cross\-functional relationships and ensuring alignment with senior stakeholders across Performance \& Brand Marketing, MarTech, Product, Sales, Analytics;
* Acting as a Thought Leader for 3 CRM Marketing Managers and Specialists, identifying key development and improvement opportunities, as well as building business cases for their implementation, followed by testing and experimentation;
* Identifying and prioritising upcoming opportunities with a data\-driven approach, deciding where to focus and building a clear technical roadmap with MarTech team;
* Fostering ongoing testing culture, assessing business impact and scaling proven solutions across markets and business units;
* Taking active part in advanced measurement and testing framework development in cooperation with analysts and data scientists;
* Developing blueprints and processes enabling a scaled approach to CRM Marketing at EU\-level.

### **What will you need to be successful in this role?**

* \>6 years of experience in Marketing \- specific CRM / Engagement / Retention / Product Marketing experience is an advantage;
* Experience in owning relationships with senior stakeholders in a cross\-functional environment;
* Experience in shaping and leading delivery of a scalable growth strategy for digital platforms and / or products across multiple markets;
* Experience working with technology and product teams on implementation projects;
* Data\-driven approach and ability to explain business impact through detailed analysis;
* Intrapreneurship, showing strong ownership and feeling comfortable to build completely new solutions, rather than focusing only on optimisation;
* Capability to work in matrix or other complex environments and ability to cope with a good degree of ambiguity;
* English fluency \- allowing you to express your thoughts smoothly and easily in an international environment.

### **What can we offer you?**

* Flexibility to work in a hybrid mode;
* Annual Bonus based on your performance;
* Customizable benefits on MyBenefit platform (e.g. Multisport card, medical package, insurance, tickets, vouchers, and many more);
* Laptop and mobile phone (per your preference);
* Open selection of training e\-courses (including but not limited to Udemy, Coursera, etc.);
* Prospective job in ones of the largest Real Estate \& Motors classifieds services;
* A team that will help you develop \& succeed;
* An environment where you will be given space to take ownership and accountability for your work;
* A company committed to building an inclusive environment for all employees and create equal opportunities;
* A great place to learn within fast\-growing, global classifieds' platforms (e.g. Otodom, Obido, OLX, Otomoto, Storia, Imovirtual, etc.).

**Diversity, Equity and Inclusion at OLX**  

At OLX, we are committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. We strongly encourage people of all races, ethnicities, disabilities, ages, gender identities or expressions, sexual orientations, religions, backgrounds, and experiences to apply.  

If you are excited about this role, and your past experiences do not align perfectly with every criteria asked for in the job description, we would still like you to apply. You may be just the right candidate for this or other opportunities across the business, and we'd like to hear from you. **Diversity, Equity and Inclusion at OLX**
OLX values diversity and welcomes applicants of all races, ethnicities, disabilities, ages, genders, sexual orientations, religions, backgrounds, and experiences to apply. If this role excites you, we encourage you to apply, even if you don’t meet all the requirements \- you may be just the right fit for this or other opportunities with us! *OLX will process your personal data to assess your fit for the applied position. You may optionally consent to store your data for up to 12 months after the application process for consideration in future OLX roles. For more details on how your application data will be processed please check our* *Privacy Statement**.*

We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.

Overview:

Groupe Dynamite Inc. (GDI) is a Montréal\-based, public company of integrated omni\-channel brands, designing and distributing accessible, trend\-forward fashion for women since 1975\.  

Our mission of "Empowering YOU to be YOU, one outfit at a time" is brought to life through the GARAGE and DYNAMITE banners and represents the consumer\-centric core of GDI's long\-standing success as a leading retailer in North America.  

Today, GDI operates nearly 300 stores across Canada and the United States, as well as shoppable brand experiences at Garageclothing.com and Dynamiteclothing.com. **Job Summary:**
Join our Data Science team, a product\-driven innovation hub reshaping the online and in\-store shopping experience. As the Data \& AI Product Lead, you’ll own the development and delivery of data science products that have real, measurable business impact. You’ll bridge the gap between business needs and technical execution, ensuring that every solution we build is deployed, adopted, and continuously improved. Working closely with colleagues across E\-commerce and brick and mortar, you’ll help bring next\-generation data products from concept to production, enhancing forecasting, allocation, and the customer experience. **Responsibilities*** Define and lead the day\-to\-day strategy and roadmap for data science products, including quarterly planning and milestone presentations;
* Translate complex business challenges into actionable product requirements and prioritize and document initiatives using Jira and Confluence;
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teammates, including data scientists, engineers, QA, analysts, and business stakeholders to bring products from concept to production;
* Own the product backlog and sprint planning to ensure alignment with Agile best practices and strategic milestones;
* Oversee the end\-to\-end lifecycle of AI and data products, ensuring quality, scalability, and successful adoption;
* Establish and track success metrics to guide post\-launch iteration and continuous improvement;
* Communicate ideas, progress, and impact clearly across both technical and business teams.

 **Qualifications*** 5\+ years of experience in product management or delivery in data/AI, with a proven track record of bringing products from development to production;
* Demonstrated ability to manage, iterate, and scale data science products to ensure lasting adoption and business impact;
* Strong hands\-on experience with Jira, Confluence, and Agile frameworks for managing product cycles;
* Solid understanding of end\-to\-end data science development workflows, including problem framing, data analysis, and performance monitoring;
* Highly organized, analytical, and outcome\-driven, with a focus on delivering measurable value;
* Exceptional communication and stakeholder management skills, comfortable translating between technical and business audiences;
* Experience in retail, fashion, or supply chain is a strong asset, but not required.



At GDI, you will be part of a growing organization that understands the importance of investing in people and offers you:* A comprehensive compensation package that includes performance\-driven bonuses;
* A group retirement savings program with employer matching;
* Flexible group insurance with personalized coverage that meets your needs;
* An employee discount at Garage and Dynamite;
* Exclusive private sample sales;
* A flexible vacation policy;
* And more!



GDI has been repeatedly voted one of Montréal’s Top Employers and one of Canada’s Top Employers for Young People. **Our promise…**  

No day will be like the last—we aim to be better today than we were yesterday. We are committed to employment equity.  

Candidates that are retained will be called for an interview.  

\#LI\-NM1
